    "scientific_verdict": "Across k in {1, 2, 3} oracle calls and prime/prime-power moduli, the matrix secret-Fourier harmonics rho_hat(delta) satisfy exact Hermitian conjugation rho_hat(-delta) = rho_hat(delta)^dagger and trace orthogonality Tr(rho_hat(delta)) = 0 for all delta != 0. The full operator Hilbert-Schmidt variance E_s[||rho(s) - rho_bar||_F^2] equals the exact purity deficit 1 - Tr(rho_bar^2) = sum_{delta != 0} ||rho_hat(delta)||_F^2 <= 1 - 1/D, which universally upper-bounds the L2 readout signal energy of any post-circuit unitary basis rotation V in U(D)."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Operator Harmonic Adjoint Symmetry and Zero-Trace Orthogonality",
      "statement": "For any k-call schedule (epsilon, sigma), the matrix secret-Fourier harmonics rho_hat_(epsilon, sigma)(delta) satisfy rho_hat(-delta mod q) = rho_hat(delta)^dagger, Tr(rho_hat(0)) = 1, and Tr(rho_hat(delta)) = 0 for all delta != 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Exact Purity-Deficit Parseval Identity for Hilbert-Schmidt Variance",
      "statement": "The full operator Hilbert-Schmidt variance V_HS(epsilon, sigma) = E_s[||rho(s) - rho_bar||_F^2] equals the exact purity deficit 1 - Tr(rho_bar^2) = sum_(delta != 0) ||rho_hat(delta)||_F^2 = sum_(delta != 0) ||M_hat(delta)||_F^2 <= 1 - 1/D."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Exact Diagonal/Off-Diagonal Conservation and Universal Unitary Readout Bound",
      "statement": "For every post-circuit unitary V in U(D), the rotated readout L2 signal energy E_(epsilon, sigma)(V) = sum_x Var_s[<x|V rho(s) V^dagger|x>] plus the non-zero harmonic off-diagonal Frobenius norm squared equals 1 - Tr(rho_bar^2), so E_(epsilon, sigma)(V) <= 1 - Tr(rho_bar^2) <= 1 - 1/D for all V in U(D)."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Native Higher-Call Commutant Trace-Orthogonality Audit: Operator Harmonic Zero-Trace Conservation, Purity-Deficit Parseval Identity, and Universal Unitary Readout Bounds"
}
